{
  "//": [
    "TIGHTENED rules — apply AFTER enabling Anonymous sign-in in the Firebase",
    "console (Authentication > Sign-in method > Anonymous > Enable).",
    "",
    "Applying these first would break 1v1 outright: every read and write starts",
    "requiring an auth that the app cannot obtain yet, and the lobby would search",
    "against a database that refuses it. Order matters — enable, verify sign-in",
    "succeeds, then publish this.",
    "",
    "What changes from firebase.rules.json: every .read and .write now demands",
    "auth != null. The shape and size checks are unchanged, because an",
    "anonymous account proves only that a real client asked, not that it asked",
    "for something reasonable. Both layers are needed.",
    "",
    "Why it matters: without this, anyone can fill /queue with tickets nobody",
    "can match. Real players then wait the full twelve-second search against",
    "opponents that do not exist, and the feature looks broken rather than",
    "attacked."
  ],
  "rules": {
    ".read": false,
    ".write": false,
    "queue": {
      ".read": "auth != null",
      "$playerId": {
        ".write": "auth != null",
        ".validate": "newData.hasChildren(['playerId','playerName','level','timestamp'])",
        "playerId": {
          ".validate": "newData.isString() && newData.val() === $playerId && newData.val().length <= 64"
        },
        "playerName": {
          ".validate": "newData.isString() && newData.val().length <= 64"
        },
        "level": {
          ".validate": "newData.isNumber() && newData.val() >= 1 && newData.val() <= 5"
        },
        "timestamp": {
          ".validate": "newData.isNumber()"
        },
        "$other": {
          ".validate": false
        }
      }
    },
    "bus": {
      ".read": "auth != null",
      "$messageId": {
        ".write": "auth != null && (!data.exists() || !newData.exists())",
        ".validate": "newData.hasChildren(['type','senderId','_ts'])",
        "type": {
          ".validate": "newData.isString() && newData.val().length <= 32"
        },
        "senderId": {
          ".validate": "newData.isString() && newData.val().length <= 64"
        },
        "_ts": {
          ".validate": "newData.isNumber()"
        },
        "roomId": {
          ".validate": "newData.isString() && newData.val().length <= 64"
        },
        "progressPct": {
          ".validate": "newData.isNumber() && newData.val() >= 0 && newData.val() <= 100"
        },
        "mistakes": {
          ".validate": "newData.isNumber() && newData.val() >= 0 && newData.val() <= 3"
        },
        "level": {
          ".validate": "newData.isNumber() && newData.val() >= 1 && newData.val() <= 5"
        },
        "$other": {
          ".validate": true
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
